userStories.description:
**Goal** — Add the shared origin vocabulary, exclude fix-gap from blocking, and round-trip non-pr origin facts through PR comments and residual summaries.

**Motivation** — Nothing in the blocking decision used the facts, so a finding in code a fix had just added blocked like a finding in the original change.

**Approach** — The origin is a reviewer judgement backed by one deterministic fact, the lineage. It is carried exactly the way the trigger class is (US-001 of #2992). The rule is fixed: `fix-gap` never blocks. There is no config key and no per-PR ruling for it (see Out of Scope).

Composition. `isBlockingFinding` applies three tests in this order, and a finding blocks only when it passes all three:
1. severity is `critical` or `important`;
2. origin is not `fix-gap` (an absent origin reads `pr`);
3. trigger is in the effective blocking trigger set (an absent trigger reads `normal`).
The order is observable only in that every combination needs all three. A `minor` `fix-regression` does not block. An `important` `pr` `adversarial` finding under the default set does not block. An `important` `fix-gap` `normal` finding does not block.

`packages/nax/src/workflow/blocking-findings/index.ts` (new exports). Target: `export const FINDING_ORIGINS = ["pr", "fix-regression", "fix-gap"] as const;`, `export type FindingOrigin = (typeof FINDING_ORIGINS)[number];`, and `export function parseFindingOrigin(value: unknown): FindingOrigin | undefined`, which returns the matching member or `undefined` for anything else.

`isBlockingFinding` (same file). Target: `isBlockingFinding(finding: { severity; trigger?; origin?: FindingOrigin }, blocking): boolean`, applying the three tests in the Composition order above. The parameter list is unchanged.

`readFindingThreadFacts` (same file). Target: returns `{ severity: WorkflowSeverity; trigger: FindingTrigger; origin: FindingOrigin }`. `origin` is read from the first line that starts `Origin:`: the text after the prefix and before the first ` - `, trimmed, passed to `parseFindingOrigin`. No such line, or an unknown value, reads `"pr"`.

`firstIssueLine` (same file). Target: also drops lines starting `Origin:`. Keep dropping `Trigger:` and `Lineage:`.

`FindingWithTrigger` and `CarriedSummary` (`packages/nax/src/bot/render-comments.ts`). Target: both gain `readonly origin?: FindingOrigin;` and `readonly originEvidence?: string;`. `residualItem` takes `CarriedSummary`, so the residual list reads the fields from there. A carried finding (`offLineFinding` in `post-carried.ts`) is built with no origin, so `### Still open from an earlier review` lines never show one.

`factLines` / `renderFindingComment` (same file). Target: when `origin` is set and is not `"pr"`, an `Origin: <origin>` line (plus ` - <originEvidence>` through `safeText(..., EVIDENCE_LIMIT)` when evidence is present) comes directly after the `Trigger:` line and before any `Lineage:` line. With no origin, or origin `"pr"`, the body is byte-identical to today's.

`residualItem` (same file, used for `### Residual findings (not blocking)` and `### Still open from an earlier review` in `renderReviewSummary`). Target: when `origin` is set and is not `"pr"`, the parenthesis gains `; origin <origin>[ - <originEvidence>]` before its closing `)`, with the evidence through `safeText(..., EVIDENCE_LIMIT)`. Otherwise the line is unchanged.

The shared predicate `isBlockingFinding` returns `false` for `fix-gap` (US-001). Every site that already asks it agrees with no further change: review posting (`collectSummaryOnly`, `blockingFindingCount`), push-worthiness (`hasPushWorthyItem`), readiness (`blockingKeys` in `fix-report.ts`), carried findings (`carried-findings.ts`, `post-carried.ts`, `carried-hold.ts`), the chain notice (`convergence-summary.ts`) and `nax workflow status` (`readBlockingFindingThreads`). Two more readers follow with no change because they ask `isBlockingFinding`: `fix-carried.ts` and `fix-facts.ts`.

**Scope** — In: shared vocabulary/predicate/thread reader, inline fact lines, residual origin clauses and tests. Extend packages/nax/test/unit/workflow/blocking-findings.test.ts and packages/nax/test/unit/bot/render-comments.test.ts; exercise readBlockingFindingThreads via its existing fixture in packages/nax/test/unit/bot/blocking-threads.test.ts for the integration-labelled reader criteria. Existing tests named US-002 AC-10 reads the severity label and the trigger line and US-002 AC-11 reads an unlabelled body as important with a normal trigger gain only `origin: "pr"` in their exact expected objects; severity and trigger expectations stay. Out: US-002 owns reviewer solicitation and reply parsing; US-003 owns lineage settlement and artifact metadata; US-004 owns earlier-thread metadata carry and readyStep scenarios. Do not add bot.blockingOrigins, writer origin rulings, new carried-record fields, fixer origin instructions or chain-notice prose.

**Interface**
```typescript
export const FINDING_ORIGINS = ["pr", "fix-regression", "fix-gap"] as const;
export type FindingOrigin = (typeof FINDING_ORIGINS)[number];
export function parseFindingOrigin(value: unknown): FindingOrigin | undefined;
// readFindingThreadFacts returns:
{ severity: WorkflowSeverity; trigger: FindingTrigger; origin: FindingOrigin }
// FindingWithTrigger and CarriedSummary each gain:
readonly origin?: FindingOrigin;
readonly originEvidence?: string;
```
